QuickJS-ng 0.15.0: MIT, bundled notice licenses/QuickJS-MIT.txt.
React 18.3.1, react-reconciler 0.29.2 and scheduler: MIT; notices accompany builds.
OpenOrbis toolchain v0.5.4 and its public graphics example informed the VideoOut
implementation. Static musl is linked under its own MIT notice; supplementary
third-party math notices are in licenses/musl-math-notices.txt. No Sony runtime
PRX/SPRX modules are copied into this package. System import stubs are link inputs.
The GPL bootstrap shims libc.prx and libSceFios2.prx are built from the tiny
OpenOrbis module sources and pinned GPL crtlib.o, not Sony's libc or FIOS runtime.
Sources: OpenOrbis-PS4-Toolchain src/modules/libc, src/modules/libSceFios2 and
src/crt/crtlib.c at b458dfd9d2f5c40aa249b127c9b9b4488afdc686. The SDK release
archive and bootstrap input hashes are recorded in the dependency locks.
The bundled 5x7 ASCII font is original project bitmap data adapted from Voidplay's
native diagnostic font, GPL-3.0-only. Manrope is baked from its SIL OFL 1.1 font;
see licenses/Manrope-OFL.txt and apps/voidplay/assets/manifest.json for provenance.
The current package icon is the existing white voidplay. wordmark on black.
The backdrop is original Voidplay concept artwork (../../docs/artwork.md).
Catalog cover credits are in apps/voidplay/assets/manifest.json. No game binaries,
downloaded game packages, or claimed authorization evidence are bundled as content.
Corresponding source/build tools are distributed in this repository; dependency
sources are pinned in dependencies.lock.json and package-lock.json. No proprietary
SDK source or executable is redistributed. Firmware compatibility remains unverified.
